## Command Resolution & Install Modes

Managed commands (`task-board`, `tb-sessiond`, `task-board-tui`) are shipped as compiled shims. Agents must resolve them shell-neutrally without assuming shell profile activation. Two install modes are supported:

- **Mode A — Curator-managed (preferred):** skill installed via `curator install` (vendored `tools/board-cli`/`tools/board-tui`, `-mod=vendor`, no network). Curator publishes project shims to `.agents/bin` and forwarding shims to `global/bin` under Curator home (e.g. `~/.local/bin`) and arranges shell integration so `PATH` contains them. Agents SHOULD invoke bare commands (`task-board`, `tb-sessiond`, `task-board-tui`) directly; the resolver below is a fallback when bare dispatch fails.

- **Mode B — Legacy / non-Curator:** no Curator environment (direct `tools/` checkout, `scripts/setup.sh`, or `PATH` not propagated / out-of-directory launch). Agents MUST use the shell-neutral resolver chain and never assume bare names:

  1. Project shim: `.agents/bin/<command>` (`.agents\bin\<command>.cmd` on Windows)
  2. Manager global shim: `global/bin` under Curator home (e.g. `~/.local/bin` forwarding shim) — covers launches outside the project root or before shell profile activation
  3. Validated bare command: `command -v <command>` on POSIX or `Get-Command <command>` on PowerShell
  4. Source-checkout fallback (last resort, not part of installed skill context): `tools/board-cli` / `tools/board-tui` build roots with `go run`/`go build -mod=vendor`

For installed skills Curator excludes build roots from skill context — use exported shims for execution and keep manifest-relative build source paths source-checkout-only. Shell profile activation is optional; prefer steps 1–3 before falling back to 4.

